' ===================== callouts =====================
note right of rchat #FEE2E2
  **No timeout on the upstream fetch (:154); no retry;
  no request-body size bound (:126).**
  A non-2xx upstream is flattened to `502 "responded with
  status N"` and the upstream error body is DISCARDED
  (:174-181), so a Pydantic 422 (bad `model`/`effort`)
  reaches the user as **"The orchestrator is unreachable"**
  via markUnreachable (streams.ts:335-337, :172-173).
  MOCK_MODE emits no `status`/`research` frames, so the
  web-search UI is untestable offline (:40-121).
end note

note right of ssel #FEE2E2
  `meta` is the ONLY event with no field validation:
  `return {kind:'meta', meta: JSON.parse(ev.data)}` (sse.ts:203)
  — while `step` and `research` are checked field-by-field.
  `meta` is what carries sql, data, chart and report_files.
  `Engine` (types.ts:8) has no `'dataset'` member although
  engines/dataset.py:101 emits `{"route":"dataset"}`.
  readChatStream's finally only releases the lock — it never
  calls reader.cancel() (sse.ts:298-300), and there is no
  idle timeout: a silent orchestrator leaves the generator
  awaiting read() forever.
end note

note bottom of streams #FEE2E2
  **Race 1 — register() overwrite (streams.ts:292).** startStream
  never checks for an existing entry; the first LiveStream's
  consume() loop keeps running with an un-aborted controller,
  hits the !sawTerminal branch (:264-268) and saveMessages()
  clobbers the newer turns in cache.
  **Race 2 — attachStream double-register**: the guard at :356
  is checked BEFORE the await at :364, and main.py:105-120
  happily serves two subscribers.
  Every non-2xx — including a 400 — becomes markUnreachable
  (:165-178). No timeout anywhere: a stream with no terminal
  frame stays `streaming` forever and Composer stays disabled.
end note

note bottom of rctl #FFFBEB
  `GET /api/chat/active` converts **every** transport failure
  into `200 {active: []}` (active/route.ts:26) — deliberate so a
  failed poll paints no error, but it also hides a permanently
  down orchestrator from the sidebar.
  `POST /api/chat/compact` runs a full LLM summarisation pass
  upstream with no timeout and no forwarded signal (:16-26).
  stopStream() aborts the local reader first and never inspects
  `{stopped}` (streams.ts:82-92) — a failed stop leaves the GPU
  generating with zero user-visible signal.
end note

note bottom of rhist #FFFBEB
  The allowlist comment at route.ts:26-27 does **not** hold:
  `encodeURIComponent('..') === '..'`, so
  `/api/history/conversations/../..` reaches the orchestrator's
  `/` and `.../../X` reaches `/history/X`.
  Blast radius is bounded (≤3 segments, embedded `/` becomes
  `%2F`, only `/history/search` exists) — not exploitable today,
  but the asserted invariant is false.
  proxy.ts buffers the whole body both ways with no size bound
  (:39, :60) — the largest is a full thread PUT carrying every
  message's `meta.data` SQL rows.
end note

note bottom of rmisc #FEE2E2
  `reports/[filename]/route.ts:20` calls `decodeURIComponent`
  **unguarded** → a malformed escape is an unhandled 500. That is
  the exact bug attach/[id]/route.ts:25-32 documents as fixed —
  the fix was never applied here.
  `GET /api/reports` (route.ts) has **no caller at all** (dead
  code) and its mock shape `Array{name,…}` disagrees with the
  real `{reports:[{filename,…}]}` and with ReportFile
  (types.ts:74-78) — three shapes for one concept.
end note

note top of browser #FEE2E2
  **TRUST BOUNDARY.** Everything inside is attacker-influenced
  (model-authored markdown, backend-supplied hrefs) and there is
  no CSP, no frame-ancestors and no img-src (next.config.mjs:1-8);
  Markdown.tsx:55-72 sets no allowedElements, so a model-authored
  image URL is a real outbound fetch.
  ORCHESTRATOR_URL is correctly server-side only — the sole
  NEXT_PUBLIC_* var is NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_NAME (layout.tsx:15).
  Every `cookie` / `set-cookie` forwarding branch in this layer
  (8 sites) is **dead code**: auth.py:89-92 never 401s, so any
  caller who can reach :3000 or :8080 reads every conversation.
end note

legend right
  |= Colour |= Layer |
  |<#2563EB> | frontend / edge (components + lib + API routes' client contract) |
  |<#7C3AED> | orchestrator / app logic (the Node-side route handlers) |
  |<#16A34A> | inference / GPU (not present at this level) |
  |<#D97706> | storage / data (localStorage only at this level) |
  |<#64748B> | external systems |
  |<#DC2626> | risk / trust boundary |
  ==Notation==
  **Thick blue arrow** = the SSE answer path, request leg and stream leg.
  **Dashed red arrow** = an unvalidated / unsafe hop.
  **Dashed red rectangle** = trust boundary.
  Amber notes = swallowed error, unbounded resource or missing timeout.
  Red notes = a defect that changes behaviour or security posture.
  Arrow labels read: protocol · payload · sync|async.
end legend

